WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.049
In total, SiT contains 60 scenes,

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:07.470
which amounts to about sixty thousand images and
twelve thousand point cloud frames,

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:13.148
carrying roughly four hundred and seventy thousand
two-dimensional annotations and three

00:00:13.228 --> 00:00:16.891
hundred and twenty thousand three-dimensional annotations.

00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:21.279
Each clip is twenty seconds of sequential data
sampled at ten hertz,

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:25.473
producing nine seconds of trajectory represented as
pose vectors.

00:00:25.553 --> 00:00:29.022
On top of this data, the paper defines four benchmarks.

00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:36.378
Three-D pedestrian detection is scored with average
precision based on center distance at thresholds of a quarter,

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:38.185
a half, one, and two meters.

00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:42.121
Three-D tracking uses standard multi-object
tracking metrics.

00:00:42.201 --> 00:00:47.800
Trajectory prediction takes two seconds of past
motion and predicts seven seconds ahead,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:53.672
scored with average and final displacement error
over the best of K candidate trajectories.

00:00:53.752 --> 00:01:00.060
And an end-to-end task runs from raw sensors all
the way to future bounding boxes and trajectories.
